{"repositoryId":736188384,"availability":"available","full":"RahulJ15/Adaptxt","name":"Adaptxt","description":"This project is a versatile Optical Character Recognition (OCR) and translation tool designed to process both images and PDF documents and leveraging NLP to translate the text into different languages and give users an option to summarize the contents of a document in their prefered language","category":"Design","language":"Python","stars":9,"forks":1,"created":"2023-12-27T08:11:18Z","updated":"2024-10-20T06:11:27Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://adaptxt.streamlit.app/","topics":["api","easyocr","extractive-summarization","google-translate-api","image-processing","ocr-recognition","summarization","tf-idf","translation"],"demo":"https://adaptxt.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T05:07:27.994Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T05:07:27.994Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T05:07:27.994Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T05:07:27.994Z","stars":9,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This project is an end-to-end Optical Character Recognition (OCR) and translation model designed to extract text from images and PDFs, and then translate it into multiple languages. The implementation is done in Python using the Tesseract OCR engine, OpenCV for image processing, Googletrans for translation, and Streamlit for the frontend."],"features":["Utilizes Tesseract OCR to extract text from images and PDFs.","Implements image preprocessing techniques, including conversion to grayscale, removal of table lines, and noise reduction, to enhance OCR accuracy.","Translates extracted text into five different languages (Hindi, French, Spanish, Mandarin, English) using the Googletrans API.","Supports PDF extraction, recognizing text from each page and translating it.","Allows the user to choose the target language for translation."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RahulJ15/Adaptxt/blob/main/REA